{{also|Divisor}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/dɪ.ˈvaɪ.zə(ɹ)/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|dĭ-vīʹ-zər}}, {{IPA|/dɨ.ˈvaɪ.zɚ/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-divisor.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
** {{homophones|diviser|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|aɪzə(r)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|arithmetic}} A number or [[expression]] that another is to be [[divide]]d by.
#: ''In "42 ÷ 3" the '''divisor''' is the 3.''
# An [[integer]] that divides another integer an [[integral]] number of times.
#: ''The positive '''divisors''' of 6 are 1, 2 and 3.''

